================================== Ai Message ==================================

<observation>================================================================================
PROTEIN EXPRESSION PERTURBATION ANALYSIS FRAMEWORK
================================================================================

TYPES OF PERTURBATIONS AND THEIR EFFECTS ON PROTEIN EXPRESSION:

Genetic:
  Description: Alterations in gene sequence or copy number
  Examples: CRISPR knockout, Gene knockdown, Overexpression, Point mutations
  Typical Effects: Loss of function, Gain of function, Altered stability

Epigenetic:
  Description: Changes in chromatin state and gene regulation
  Examples: DNA methylation, Histone modification, Chromatin remodeling
  Typical Effects: Gene silencing, Transcriptional activation, Altered accessibility

Transcriptional:
  Description: Modulation of transcription factors and regulatory elements
  Examples: TF knockdown, Promoter mutation, Enhancer deletion
  Typical Effects: Reduced mRNA, Altered splicing, Changed expression kinetics

Post-transcriptional:
  Description: Changes in RNA processing and stability
  Examples: miRNA inhibition, RNA degradation, Alternative splicing
  Typical Effects: mRNA instability, Reduced translation, Isoform shifts

Translational:
  Description: Alterations in protein synthesis
  Examples: Ribosome inhibition, tRNA depletion, Codon optimization
  Typical Effects: Reduced protein synthesis, Altered protein folding

Post-translational:
  Description: Modifications after protein synthesis
  Examples: Phosphorylation, Ubiquitination, Proteolysis
  Typical Effects: Activation/inactivation, Localization change, Protein degradation

Environmental:
  Description: External conditions affecting expression
  Examples: Temperature, Nutrient starvation, Hypoxia, Drug treatment
  Typical Effects: Stress response, Metabolic remodeling, Cell fate change

</observation>
