├─ mRNA: Undetectable (<5%)
├─ Protein: Undetectable
├─ Viability: >90%
├─ Phenotype: Subtle or none
└─ Timeline: 48-72h to full effect

Scenario 2: CRISPR Knockout of Essential Gene
├─ mRNA: Undetectable
├─ Protein: Undetectable
├─ Viability: Reduced (50-80%)
├─ Phenotype: Cell death, apoptosis
└─ Timeline: Progressive decline 48-96h

Scenario 3: Drug Treatment (On-target)
├─ mRNA: Variable (depends on mechanism)
├─ Protein: Reduced or modified
├─ Viability: Dose-dependent
├─ Phenotype: Rapid (hours to days)
└─ Timeline: 30min to 24h

Scenario 4: Environmental Stress
├─ mRNA: Stress genes ↑, housekeeping ↓
├─ Protein: HSP ↑, metabolic proteins ↓
├─ Viability: Reduced over time
├─ Phenotype: Metabolic adaptation
└─ Timeline: 1-6h response, 24+h adaptation

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

DIRECT VS INDIRECT EFFECTS:

Direct Effects (Target these first)
├─ Immediate response (0-2h)
├─ Strong fold-change (>2-fold)
├─ Consistent across replicates
├─ Identified with early timepoints
└─ Example: Target gene mRNA drops within 2h of CRISPR

Primary Indirect Effects
├─ Early response (2-8h)
├─ Moderate fold-change (1-2 fold)
├─ Downstream of direct targets
├─ Identified with 4-8h timepoints
└─ Example: mRNA of genes regulated by target protein

Secondary Indirect Effects
├─ Late response (24+h)
├─ Variable direction (up or down)
├─ Compensatory mechanisms
├─ Identified with late timepoints
└─ Example: Upregulation of paralog genes

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

TROUBLESHOOTING:

Problem: No effect observed
→ Check: Perturbation efficiency, cell health, measurement method
→ Solution: Verify knockdown >70%, use more sensitive detection

Problem: Unexpected cell death
→ Check: Off-target effects, stress markers, cell viability
→ Solution: Validate specificity, check for stress response

Problem: Inconsistent replicates
→ Check: Batch effects, technical variation, data quality
→ Solution: Normalize across batches, increase replicates

Problem: Results don't match literature
→ Check: Cell type, conditions, measurement method
→ Solution: Test in same cell type, compare methods

